WEBVTT

00:03.900 --> 00:05.569
That was a solid hit.

00:05.570 --> 00:07.529
You can hit off that pitcher.

00:07.530 --> 00:08.989
Yeah?

00:08.990 --> 00:09.990
Yeah.

00:10.200 --> 00:11.910
They're still kids.

00:14.830 --> 00:16.909
You look pretty unhappy there, Captain.

00:16.910 --> 00:19.789
You really think Harada can
be hit off that easily, Shun?

00:19.790 --> 00:21.290
Sorry,

00:21.670 --> 00:24.709
but I'm going to gobble
up your pretty little princess.

00:24.710 --> 00:25.759
What?

00:25.760 --> 00:29.509
I don't think he's going to
last until your next at-bat.

00:29.510 --> 00:31.470
Shun, cut it out!

00:49.110 --> 00:54.660
I've heard it said so many times

00:55.410 --> 01:01.580
How it's not going to work out

01:02.540 --> 01:08.090
That nothing will change

01:08.380 --> 01:14.550
Even if I pretended not to listen

01:15.010 --> 01:18.389
I knew it all

01:18.390 --> 01:21.559
I learned this from you

01:21.560 --> 01:29.560
That it's not a failure, even when it is

01:30.950 --> 01:37.539
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

01:37.540 --> 01:44.459
The quiet melodies push me forward

01:44.460 --> 01:50.969
Because the sky is so vast and free

01:50.970 --> 01:58.600
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

02:08.520 --> 02:10.229
Can't hit over there.

02:10.230 --> 02:11.030
Out three! Change sides!

02:11.031 --> 02:12.399
Make sure to keep that in mind!

02:12.400 --> 02:13.400
Right!

02:14.280 --> 02:16.909
Shuugo, your princess is done for.

02:16.910 --> 02:19.159
He'll be lucky to last until next inning.

02:19.160 --> 02:20.290
He's way too fragile.

02:22.790 --> 02:25.420
And how can you tell that, exactly?!

02:26.170 --> 02:28.290
How can you not, idiot?!

02:29.090 --> 02:33.839
Basically, you're only thinking about
that date you had with the princess.

02:33.840 --> 02:36.300
That's why you can't tell anything.

02:36.680 --> 02:39.809
Is Nitta East really that bad of a team?

02:39.810 --> 02:43.060
Don't ask me such a
basic question so seriously.

02:43.730 --> 02:45.650
They aren't bad.

02:47.810 --> 02:50.820
But that battery is an issue.

02:51.230 --> 02:53.530
The princess and the giant catcher.

02:54.070 --> 02:55.700
You couldn't do much worse.

02:56.320 --> 02:57.950
- Yokote Second
- Yokote Second

02:56.320 --> 02:57.950
- Nitta East
- Nitta East

03:05.750 --> 03:08.539
Jouno, don't get tricked by the speed.

03:08.540 --> 03:09.880
Just try to get a piece of it.

03:10.170 --> 03:11.709
I know you'll be able to hit it.

03:11.710 --> 03:12.710
Right.

03:16.550 --> 03:17.680
All right.

03:18.140 --> 03:20.510
Is he having an off day or something?

03:23.430 --> 03:28.019
Why are you worrying about the opposing
pitcher's condition during our game?

03:28.020 --> 03:33.150
Like I said, it's the battery that's
the problem, not the princess.

03:33.440 --> 03:34.989
What do you mean?

03:34.990 --> 03:36.650
I'm not surprised.

03:37.820 --> 03:38.910
You wouldn't understand.

03:51.920 --> 03:52.920
Yokote Second

03:52.921 --> 03:53.921
Nitta East

03:57.430 --> 03:58.680
Good one, Hagi!

04:03.180 --> 04:04.270
All right.

04:05.850 --> 04:08.690
He's a mess mentally right now.

04:09.020 --> 04:12.149
He has no idea what he needs to throw.

04:12.150 --> 04:14.190
Yet we still can't hit a home run.

04:14.480 --> 04:17.200
Our batters are barely able to get singles.

04:17.530 --> 04:19.109
That's quite the princess.

04:19.110 --> 04:21.570
So why is the princess getting hit off of?

04:26.580 --> 04:29.789
You're a batter, unlike him.

04:29.790 --> 04:32.080
Unfortunately, your princess is a pitcher.

04:32.500 --> 04:37.089
Pitchers can't do anything when
they don't have a catcher to catch.

04:37.090 --> 04:39.679
Just tell me, Shun. Why...

04:39.680 --> 04:41.340
Just concentrate on the game.

04:42.140 --> 04:43.140
Ball four.

04:46.350 --> 04:48.729
See, Ikebe walked.

04:48.730 --> 04:50.269
That was four straight balls.

04:50.270 --> 04:55.360
How could a guy with such great control
not be able to throw a single strike?

04:55.650 --> 04:58.030
Your princess is on life support.

05:02.030 --> 05:03.870
They're swapping out their whole battery?

05:04.660 --> 05:09.370
Kaionji is coaching with way more
composure than you, you know.

05:16.880 --> 05:19.630
Wow, that really hit you hard.

05:20.300 --> 05:23.890
It was the first time I've
ever met someone like him.

05:24.850 --> 05:26.890
This might be it for him.

05:27.180 --> 05:31.389
At the very least, your princess is gonna
need some time to return to the mound.

05:31.390 --> 05:32.689
Is that what you think?

05:32.690 --> 05:34.859
Without a doubt.

05:34.860 --> 05:38.110
Guys like him are stupid fragile.

05:39.360 --> 05:40.900
Out three! Change sides!

05:41.780 --> 05:43.489
It's time for us to go out.

05:43.490 --> 05:44.739
What? Why?!

05:44.740 --> 05:47.410
Sakiyama grounded out to short.

05:47.700 --> 05:49.160
It was a double play.

05:49.620 --> 05:52.329
Damn. What are we gonna do?

05:52.330 --> 05:55.289
You're gonna have to bat next inning.

05:55.290 --> 05:56.459
What do you mean?

05:56.460 --> 05:58.299
They pulled the princess out.

05:58.300 --> 06:00.589
I figured your heart wouldn't be in it.

06:00.590 --> 06:04.179
You're not gonna ask
for a pinch hitter, are you?

06:04.180 --> 06:05.680
Screw you, man!

06:11.480 --> 06:12.180
Crap!

06:12.181 --> 06:14.189
What the hell are you boys doing?!

06:14.190 --> 06:16.440
Damn! We're busted!

06:17.940 --> 06:19.439
What do you mean?

06:19.440 --> 06:21.609
We're just playing a game, Coach.

06:21.610 --> 06:23.069
Don't give me that!

06:23.070 --> 06:25.029
The school never gave
you permission for this!

06:25.030 --> 06:27.829
You think you can just put this
game together on your own?!

06:27.830 --> 06:30.329
But it's Sunday, sir.

06:30.330 --> 06:32.080
We're doing this on our free time.

06:32.370 --> 06:36.459
Don't give me that free time excuse
when you're wearing Yokote's uniform!

06:36.460 --> 06:37.630
Excuse me.

06:38.880 --> 06:40.340
My name is Tomura.

06:40.670 --> 06:43.170
I'm Nitta East's coach.

06:47.350 --> 06:48.969
Do you think we can continue?

06:48.970 --> 06:51.349
Doubt it. Game's a forfeit.

06:51.350 --> 06:54.849
Looks like our coach is real pissed off.

06:54.850 --> 06:56.229
I can't believe this is happening.

06:56.230 --> 06:58.229
We're having such a good game.

06:58.230 --> 07:00.439
Sorry about this. I'll
try talking to Coach.

07:00.440 --> 07:01.529
Don't waste your time.

07:01.530 --> 07:03.240
Besides, look how scared everyone is.

07:03.690 --> 07:05.199
Let's just call it a day.

07:05.200 --> 07:07.869
Well, I'm sorry for all the
trouble we've caused you.

07:07.870 --> 07:09.779
So, what are we doing after this?

07:09.780 --> 07:10.280
Huh?

07:10.281 --> 07:13.539
Kadowaki here hasn't had his fill.

07:13.540 --> 07:17.169
He can't sleep because he dreams
about his beloved princess every night.

07:17.170 --> 07:18.419
Don't you feel sorry for him?

07:18.420 --> 07:19.130
What?

07:19.131 --> 07:20.380
Cut it out already!

07:20.710 --> 07:24.130
I know you don't want to just
leave things like this, Kaionji.

07:24.420 --> 07:26.339
Have another game with us.

07:26.340 --> 07:27.839
But...

07:27.840 --> 07:35.139
It was fun, getting to play a team we
wanted to instead of one the school picked.

07:35.140 --> 07:36.809
Yeah, it was.

07:36.810 --> 07:38.059
So let's do this again.

07:38.060 --> 07:39.479
It doesn't have to be soon.

07:39.480 --> 07:41.360
We can wait until after our exams.

07:42.650 --> 07:43.899
Okay.

07:43.900 --> 07:45.399
I think we'd all like that.

07:45.400 --> 07:47.150
We have a deal!

07:47.570 --> 07:49.819
But there's one condition.

07:49.820 --> 07:50.740
One condition?

07:50.741 --> 07:54.410
You have to promise to let
the princess take the mound.

07:55.660 --> 07:57.419
You mean Harada?

07:57.420 --> 08:01.039
Kaionji, could you look the
other way for me for a second?

08:01.040 --> 08:01.960
Huh?

08:01.961 --> 08:03.209
Please.

08:03.210 --> 08:04.210
Okay.

08:06.590 --> 08:09.090
Why did we lose?

08:12.970 --> 08:14.810
Gou, it's Kadowaki.

08:21.270 --> 08:22.310
Harada.

08:23.570 --> 08:24.570
Yes?

08:26.440 --> 08:27.700
Don't give me that!

08:30.570 --> 08:32.449
Are you screwing with me?!

08:32.450 --> 08:35.700
What the hell was that
pitching after all that talk?!

08:37.330 --> 08:41.079
Do you understand that you
just got dragged off the mound?!

08:41.080 --> 08:44.460
Kadowaki, you can't
do this to our teammate!

08:47.170 --> 08:51.180
You think you won because you
managed to strike one of us out once?!

08:52.300 --> 08:56.220
Do you have any idea how
pathetic you were out there today?!

08:56.850 --> 08:58.230
I do.

08:58.850 --> 09:01.230
Nagakura, was it?

09:01.520 --> 09:03.729
I'm Mizugaki.

09:03.730 --> 09:06.230
How long have you known the princess here?

09:07.280 --> 09:09.859
We met this past March.

09:09.860 --> 09:12.069
So it's only been six months?

09:12.070 --> 09:15.529
Then I guess you wouldn't
know how to get along yet.

09:15.530 --> 09:18.869
Mizugaki, do you remember
what you said in the batter's box?

09:18.870 --> 09:20.870
What? Did I say something?

09:22.920 --> 09:24.880
You told me I couldn't catch for him.

09:25.210 --> 09:26.879
What did you mean by that?

09:26.880 --> 09:28.549
I meant exactly that.

09:28.550 --> 09:31.130
You're not fit to be
the princess's catcher.

09:31.590 --> 09:33.550
You're just dragging him down.

09:34.390 --> 09:38.890
With someone like the princess,
you need a catcher that can go toe-to-toe.

09:39.560 --> 09:42.900
When you've got one like you
who's desperately trying to keep up,

09:44.060 --> 09:45.400
it'll eventually fall apart.

09:45.900 --> 09:48.069
And look where that got you today.

09:48.070 --> 09:51.900
If you two stay a battery,
you'll only destroy yourselves.

09:52.660 --> 09:58.910
And as for me, I've been playing baseball with
this wonder kid called Kadowaki Shuugo for years.

10:01.910 --> 10:04.540
Hurry up, you two! We're leaving!

10:04.880 --> 10:07.289
Come on, Shuugo. We're done here.

10:07.290 --> 10:10.800
Sorry, Princess. Pitch
to us again sometime.

10:11.420 --> 10:14.010
Assuming you're not too scared to.

10:29.610 --> 10:30.440
Let's go.

10:30.441 --> 10:31.609
Nagakura.

10:31.610 --> 10:32.360
Sir?

10:32.361 --> 10:35.199
You don't have to run. Hang back here.

10:35.200 --> 10:36.659
The rest of you go running.

10:36.660 --> 10:37.660
Yes, sir.

10:37.990 --> 10:39.030
Coach?

10:39.700 --> 10:40.700
Get in position.

10:41.200 --> 10:43.210
I'll pitch to you.

10:50.050 --> 10:51.460
I'm not holding back.

11:02.930 --> 11:04.020
How was that?

11:04.940 --> 11:05.940
Sir.

11:06.600 --> 11:08.479
I think they're powerful pitches.

11:08.480 --> 11:10.479
How do they stack up?

11:10.480 --> 11:11.280
What?

11:11.281 --> 11:14.240
I'm asking you how they
stack up to his pitches.

11:14.780 --> 11:15.910
To Takumi's?

11:16.700 --> 11:20.279
You pitch like a fielder, sir.

11:20.280 --> 11:22.239
I can't really compare it to him.

11:22.240 --> 11:24.369
Okay, that's all then.

11:24.370 --> 11:28.580
I'll have him pitch at seventy percent.

11:29.340 --> 11:32.209
That's what I'll tell him
when he's finished his test.

11:32.210 --> 11:37.219
I'll tell him to learn how to pitch
around their batting at seventy percent.

11:37.220 --> 11:40.850
Then someone other than
you can still catch for him.

11:41.260 --> 11:44.849
Are you going to tell Takumi
not to pitch his hardest?

11:44.850 --> 11:49.860
If I don't, he won't be able
to get back on the mound.

11:50.770 --> 11:52.899
I don't think he would agree to that.

11:52.900 --> 11:53.900
No?

11:54.440 --> 11:58.279
He might ask me to let him
back on the mound, actually.

11:58.280 --> 12:02.369
He hasn't been doing a lot of pitching
practice in the month since that game.

12:02.370 --> 12:04.909
I think he might be at his limit.

12:04.910 --> 12:08.620
If you can't be his catcher,
I'm still going to get him to pitch.

12:09.080 --> 12:12.630
Even at seventy percent,
he should be able to take on most teams.

12:14.170 --> 12:17.129
Do you want to quit, Nagakura?

12:17.130 --> 12:19.389
It wouldn't be too late.

12:19.390 --> 12:24.890
No matter how hard you work or how much you
struggle, Harada probably won't help you.

12:27.020 --> 12:28.689
You don't understand.

12:28.690 --> 12:29.690
What?

12:30.060 --> 12:32.480
You don't understand anything, Coach.

12:33.650 --> 12:34.650
I...

12:36.780 --> 12:38.400
Sorry. I shouldn't've said that.

12:38.700 --> 12:42.700
Your decision to quit is your own to make.

12:48.830 --> 12:50.039
Phone for you, Bro.

12:50.040 --> 12:51.040
Huh?

12:52.330 --> 12:54.339
They sounded busy.

12:54.340 --> 12:55.670
What's that mean?

12:56.130 --> 12:56.960
Hello?

12:56.961 --> 12:58.589
<i>It's me.</i>

12:58.590 --> 12:59.629
Who is this?

12:59.630 --> 13:01.179
<i>It's Yoshisada.</i>

13:01.180 --> 13:02.969
<i>The handsome and cool Yoshisada.</i>

13:02.970 --> 13:04.309
Oh.

13:04.310 --> 13:06.389
I'll be over at your house soon.

13:06.390 --> 13:07.390
See you then.

13:09.390 --> 13:11.849
Apparently, we're getting
some unwelcome company.

13:11.850 --> 13:13.439
Is Gou coming?

13:13.440 --> 13:14.440
No.

13:15.570 --> 13:17.399
I miss Gou.

13:17.400 --> 13:18.569
Shut up.

13:18.570 --> 13:21.570
Don't you feel lonely?

13:24.870 --> 13:27.290
I've got some big news today.

13:29.660 --> 13:31.619
Then please keep it short.

13:31.620 --> 13:33.380
And don't lay down on my bed.

13:33.830 --> 13:37.000
The captain asked me if
I wanted to play catcher.

13:39.340 --> 13:42.129
So, what did you say?

13:42.130 --> 13:44.049
I told him no way.

13:44.050 --> 13:48.389
I mean, from a baseball standpoint,
I understand that I'm the last hope.

13:48.390 --> 13:49.729
Well, I don't!

13:49.730 --> 13:51.189
It has to be Gou!

13:51.190 --> 13:53.149
Why are they even talking to you?

13:53.150 --> 13:56.319
Hey, I don't want to
catch for Harada either.

13:56.320 --> 13:58.399
Besides, playing catcher's so boring.

13:58.400 --> 14:00.529
You're constantly standing and sitting.

14:00.530 --> 14:04.159
Also, having to hide my beautiful
face behind a mask is such a crime.

14:04.160 --> 14:07.699
Don't tell me you said all
this to Captain Nonomura.

14:07.700 --> 14:10.539
I turned down the captain
and coach very clearly.

14:10.540 --> 14:14.459
I can't believe you said all that
to Otomurai. You're so stupid.

14:14.460 --> 14:16.040
Yet I'm somehow still impressed.

14:19.920 --> 14:20.920
Harada.

14:21.590 --> 14:22.590
It's Gou.

14:34.140 --> 14:35.140
Gou.

14:37.110 --> 14:38.110
<i>Takumi.</i>

14:39.570 --> 14:41.070
<i>Is Yoshisada gonna catch for you?</i>

14:53.210 --> 14:53.710
Idiot!

14:53.710 --> 14:54.710
Ow.

14:55.080 --> 14:56.999
Why didn't you say anything?

14:57.000 --> 14:59.089
Did you forget how to talk?

14:59.090 --> 15:02.710
You could've told him you wanted
to play baseball with him, idiot!

15:07.720 --> 15:09.969
Not that I care...

15:09.970 --> 15:13.179
Only the princess can say he won that game.

15:13.180 --> 15:13.980
Harada?

15:13.980 --> 15:14.940
Yeah.

15:14.941 --> 15:19.149
I mean, he definitely beat
Kadowaki. That's really something.

15:19.150 --> 15:21.979
Whatever happens after, he still has that.

15:21.980 --> 15:22.900
Mizugaki.

15:22.900 --> 15:23.530
Hm?

15:23.531 --> 15:25.989
Did you say something to Nagakura?

15:25.990 --> 15:29.779
What? Has he been too busy moping
around to come to practice or something?

15:29.780 --> 15:34.619
He's been going to practice, but he
doesn't even try to catch for Harada.

15:34.620 --> 15:36.289
I think that's fine.

15:36.290 --> 15:39.839
I'm sure the princess is too scared
to get back on the mound anyway.

15:39.840 --> 15:41.879
No, Harada's fine.

15:41.880 --> 15:45.509
But there's no point if
Nagakura isn't catching for him.

15:45.510 --> 15:46.759
What?

15:46.760 --> 15:49.009
The princess is still pitching?

15:49.010 --> 15:52.099
I'm talking about Nagakura right now.

15:52.100 --> 15:55.060
Why do you keep talking about Harada?

15:57.270 --> 16:03.279
Before the game even began,
Kadowaki looked really insecure.

16:03.280 --> 16:08.489
I don't think he even realized it himself, but
he was questioning if he could hit the ball.

16:08.490 --> 16:09.780
Caught me by surprise.

16:10.530 --> 16:14.540
I was curious to learn more about the
guy who could rattle Kadowaki like that.

16:15.200 --> 16:20.419
And then I see his princess standing on the mound
looking like it's just another day at the park.

16:20.420 --> 16:23.299
The battle was over before
he even threw out the first pitch.

16:23.300 --> 16:26.299
A second showdown would've
ended with the same result.

16:26.300 --> 16:30.219
So that's why you messed with
Nagakura to break up the battery.

16:30.220 --> 16:32.300
Now, that's hardly a fair accusation.

16:32.600 --> 16:35.810
It was pretty clear that
Nagakura was barely hanging on.

16:36.520 --> 16:39.439
Anyway, forget about your battery.

16:39.440 --> 16:41.019
I just wanted to confirm it one last time.

16:41.020 --> 16:44.609
We want to do this as soon
as we can after the exams.

16:44.610 --> 16:47.189
We'll need an adult
to reserve a field for us.

16:47.190 --> 16:49.399
I'll talk to our coach about that.

16:49.400 --> 16:51.949
Really? You can trust him?

16:51.950 --> 16:53.579
I think we can.

16:53.580 --> 16:59.749
Well, our coach almost burst a
blood vessel from our little game.

16:59.750 --> 17:01.209
Sorry for all the trouble.

17:01.210 --> 17:02.379
For who?

17:02.380 --> 17:04.839
You don't gotta worry about Shuugo.

17:04.840 --> 17:07.210
He's got his scholarship.

17:07.630 --> 17:09.049
Mizugaki, do you...

17:09.050 --> 17:10.050
What?

17:10.680 --> 17:12.720
Do you hate Kadowaki or something?

17:16.220 --> 17:17.980
Where do you come off saying that?!

17:18.350 --> 17:19.980
Why would I...

17:20.390 --> 17:22.440
It just seemed that way.

17:23.150 --> 17:24.150
Sorry.

17:25.730 --> 17:26.980
Whatever. Later.

17:38.870 --> 17:41.079
<i>Shun? Where are you?</i>

17:41.080 --> 17:42.709
Guess.

17:42.710 --> 17:43.540
<i>Nitta?</i>

17:43.541 --> 17:45.919
Wow, got it right on the
first try! How did you know?

17:45.920 --> 17:47.500
<i>What are you doing there?</i>

17:47.880 --> 17:51.759
I met up with Kaionji to
talk about our rematch.

17:51.760 --> 17:52.969
<i>Is it going to happen?</i>

17:52.970 --> 17:54.179
For sure.

17:54.180 --> 17:57.139
I'm not gonna screw it up like you did.

17:57.140 --> 17:59.179
I'll set the perfect stage for you.

17:59.180 --> 18:00.180
<i>Oh?</i>

18:00.730 --> 18:03.769
I mean, it's going to be the
last game I'll get to play with you.

18:03.770 --> 18:05.770
<i>Huh? What are you talking about?</i>

18:06.230 --> 18:08.320
Well, the thing is...

18:09.530 --> 18:11.989
What exactly were you thinking?

18:11.990 --> 18:14.949
Shuugo?! Why the hell are you here?!

18:14.950 --> 18:18.290
I got a hunch when I heard
you left early this morning.

18:25.420 --> 18:27.629
Gou, we have visitors.

18:27.630 --> 18:28.799
For me?

18:28.800 --> 18:30.339
Yes, it's Harada.

18:30.340 --> 18:31.469
Takumi's here?

18:31.470 --> 18:32.879
No, it's Seiha.

18:32.880 --> 18:34.680
Sawaguchi and Higashidani are here too.

18:38.140 --> 18:40.559
Gou, I brought you some potatoes!

18:40.560 --> 18:41.430
Potatoes?

18:41.431 --> 18:43.689
It was so weird!

18:43.690 --> 18:49.439
When I came to bring you these potatoes, I
saw all of them pacing in front of your house.

18:49.440 --> 18:51.070
So then we all came in together.

18:52.070 --> 18:54.070
Gou, we came to get you.

18:54.450 --> 18:56.619
Let's play!

18:56.620 --> 18:57.819
Play?

18:57.820 --> 18:59.449
Play what?

18:59.450 --> 19:00.659
Baseball!

19:00.660 --> 19:01.660
Baseball?

19:01.661 --> 19:03.080
Come on, Gou!

19:03.410 --> 19:04.999
Harada's waiting for you at the park.

19:05.000 --> 19:07.749
He seriously can't do anything.

19:07.750 --> 19:11.250
He couldn't even come
to get you. It's pathetic.

19:12.550 --> 19:15.589
You seriously can't do anything, Harada.

19:15.590 --> 19:17.719
What are you, some kind of prince?

19:17.720 --> 19:20.599
Can you really get through
life with so few life skills?

19:20.600 --> 19:23.979
You should've been the
one to go to Nagakura's place.

19:23.980 --> 19:28.110
I mean, I don't really get
why he's been so mopey.

19:29.270 --> 19:31.109
Hey, are you even listening?

19:31.110 --> 19:33.649
Look, it's fine to be cool.

19:33.650 --> 19:35.610
But Nagakura's your friend, right?

19:36.950 --> 19:38.659
He's not a friend.

19:38.660 --> 19:39.989
Harada!

19:39.990 --> 19:42.539
How could you just say that so casually?

19:42.540 --> 19:46.789
So what? Is he just some sort
of catching machine to you then?

19:46.790 --> 19:49.130
You'll just toss him
aside if he can't do that?

19:49.580 --> 19:53.129
I mean, he doesn't look
at me as a friend either.

19:53.130 --> 19:56.880
Oh, man. Could you have
said anything more sad?

19:59.890 --> 20:01.260
Guess who.

20:01.930 --> 20:04.430
Ow...

20:05.640 --> 20:07.979
Jeez, what a grip.

20:07.980 --> 20:11.859
A princess shouldn't be violent, you know.

20:11.860 --> 20:12.939
Mizugaki.

20:12.940 --> 20:13.940
What's up?

20:13.941 --> 20:17.199
Could you stop calling me a princess?

20:17.200 --> 20:20.739
Yeah, I'm the only one
who gets to tease Harada.

20:20.740 --> 20:21.949
You guys back off!

20:21.950 --> 20:25.659
Well now, who is this
Kurinosuke we've got here?

20:25.660 --> 20:27.709
You should treat your
upperclassmen with respect.

20:27.710 --> 20:30.709
Guys from other schools
can't be your upperclassmen.

20:30.710 --> 20:31.959
They're just geezers.

20:31.960 --> 20:33.710
This guy is starting to piss me off.

20:34.550 --> 20:35.959
What's so funny?

20:35.960 --> 20:41.969
Oh, I just never imagined I'd meet someone
here who could keep up with your mouth.

20:41.970 --> 20:43.389
I'm Yoshisada.

20:43.390 --> 20:45.469
You'll be Kurinosuke.

20:45.470 --> 20:47.599
We just stopped by Harada's house.

20:47.600 --> 20:52.980
They told us he was here, so we came
by to see how the princess was doing.

20:55.980 --> 20:59.240
How is Nitta East's battery doing?

21:08.660 --> 21:11.000
I want another shot in the spring.

21:11.580 --> 21:14.499
You mean a game?

21:14.500 --> 21:15.500
Yes.

21:15.840 --> 21:16.960
We're doing it again.

21:17.630 --> 21:18.630
That okay?

21:21.760 --> 21:24.115
Summer's peak came and went

21:26.470 --> 21:32.809
That's what the weather report said

21:32.810 --> 21:39.320
But it still feels like
the city is restless

21:47.160 --> 21:55.160
The evening bells of 5 p.m.
resonate inside my heart today

22:02.090 --> 22:08.495
Clouding me with something
convenient like "destiny"

22:20.466 --> 22:24.159
It's the final fireworks of the year

22:24.160 --> 22:27.870
I will remember them for years to come

22:27.871 --> 22:31.579
I will remember them for years to come

22:31.580 --> 22:33.415
Are you here? You're probably not

22:33.416 --> 22:35.249
Are you here? You're probably not

22:35.250 --> 22:37.150
I'm sure you're not

22:37.151 --> 22:39.049
I'm sure you're not

22:39.050 --> 22:40.860
Will I be able to say it if I see you?

22:40.861 --> 22:42.669
Will I be able to say it if I see you?

22:42.670 --> 22:45.490
I close my eyes and dream

22:45.491 --> 22:48.310
I close my eyes and dream

22:53.730 --> 22:54.769
<i>Takumi.</i>

22:54.770 --> 22:56.439
<i>The captain wants you.</i>

22:56.440 --> 22:57.440
<i>Let's go.</i>

22:58.030 --> 22:58.740
<i>Yo.</i>

22:58.741 --> 23:00.570
<i>It feels like it's been a long time.</i>

23:02.620 --> 23:04.579
<i>Who's a starter now?</i>

23:04.580 --> 23:05.869
<i>Stop making things up.</i>

23:05.870 --> 23:07.869
<i>Are you stupid? Everyone's saying it.</i>

23:07.870 --> 23:09.710
<i>Nobody says that!</i>

23:12.790 --> 23:15.749
<i>I don't want to grow older.</i>

23:15.750 --> 23:18.670
<i>You shouldn't be saying
that until you hit twenty.</i>

23:19.510 --> 23:20.510
<i>I really don't want that.</i>

23:20.680 --> 23:23.640
I wish I could play baseball forever.

23:23.641 --> 23:27.010
Episode 9: "Throwing Home"

23:24.760 --> 23:26.100
Let's play!
